'''Solís''' ([[Baliscano language|Baliscano]] for "sun") is a [[Planned communities in Balisca|planned community]] under development since 1983 in the [[Xaraba]] region of [[Bayara]], located roughly halfway between [[Calatayud]] and [[Vilaxoyosa]] on the [[Western Plains (Balisca)|Western Plains]]. The commune spans an area of {{Convert|50|km2|sqmi}}, and houses approximately 283,457 people as of April 2025. The city plans to house 300,000 people by 2027, with aims to accommodate double that amount at some point in the future.

The city is be connected to existing urban areas via the [[Autopista of Balisca|''autopista'']], [[W:Commuter rail|commuter]] and [[AVB|high-speed rail]]. Solís hosts the headquarters of the [[Association of Baliscan Urban Planners|Asociación de Planificadors Ciudatans de Baliscan]] (APCB). The city is designed to be a hub for {{W|cleantech}} companies. It's first tenant was the [[Solís Institute of Technology]] (SIT), which has been operating in the city since it moved into its campus in June 2015.

Solís is designed to be pedestrian and cyclist-oriented, with a large residential population living in the city centre with {{W|mixed-use development}}s, typically with a medium-height/density with a commercial base and residential units on top. There is significant reliance on {{W|mass public transit}}, along with the maintenance of green park spaces, and increasing tree cover. Private vehicle ownership is heavily discouraged, and the majority of private vehicles are restricted outside of the city center.{{Balisca articles}}
